{"id": "EUVD-2026-76280", "enisaUuid": "2443f15b-1e0c-3b4a-95c1-3cea34947761", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndm-pcache: detect a cycle in the last-kset chain during replay\n\ncache_replay() follows the on-media last-kset chain by next_cache_seg_id\nwith no cond_resched(). A forged chain that points back into a segment it\nhas already visited makes the replay loop follow it forever.\n\nCap the last-kset hops at cache->n_segs; a valid chain visits each segment\nat most once.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/663ee2f3824a505b983162de44134e789f8230da", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5311dfc5cd70edccd110257e3f30b2c1dcd3768d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16c3b3a326e70f246a605b3dc27b7f83ba4743e3"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p2v2-4gmp-9rph", "CVE-2026-80957"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2c00919f-2c75-3bae-a103-9a4e56f72e29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <16c3b3a326e70f246a605b3dc27b7f83ba4743e3"}, {"id": "56ae1327-35ed-3370-a6d8-8f66d535f055", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "56ea5fb1-b05d-3990-92fb-72e09ce90a65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "787c80bb-b8a7-3208-9c65-8a4df64e2278", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <663ee2f3824a505b983162de44134e789f8230da"}, {"id": "c1e18d05-c68a-3ab8-be6c-5bb143e8ec35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d57628ff95b32d5cfa8d8f50e07690c161e9cf0 <5311dfc5cd70edccd110257e3f30b2c1dcd3768d"}, {"id": "c81a4876-cf32-3ebc-b7ff-9ee6b92b8e0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "L